# Nmap Lab Report

## 1. Objective

To learn how to use Nmap to perform basic network scanning and identify the status of TCP ports.

## 2. Lab Environment

* Operating System: Kali Linux
* Tool: Nmap
* Platform: VirtualBox

## 3. Commands Used

```bash
nmap 127.0.0.1
nmap -sV 127.0.0.1
nmap -p- 127.0.0.1
nmap -O 127.0.0.1
```

## 4. Results

The scans completed successfully. The host was reachable, and the scan displayed the status of the scanned TCP ports.

## 5. Observations

I learned how to perform basic scans, interpret Nmap output, and understand the difference between open and closed ports.

## 6. Conclusion

This lab introduced me to Nmap and its basic scanning capabilities. It improved my understanding of network reconnaissance in a controlled lab environment.
